{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner read checker 7ea5 in full, complete retained d49-vs-first draft U3, d49 records 825–896 and factory/handoff/receipt/read sections 1001–1142, and complete actual bytes/domains.ts plus contract/intent.ts. This is selected draft feedback, not fresh complete 1415-line DESIGN or frozen-byte adoption. Resolve the four remaining exactness choices in the same successor.\n\nAcceptance has no extra idempotencyKey field. Its replay identity is the external digest of its exact payload in artroom-site-handoff-acceptance-1 framing; signature/envelope bytes are retained separately. The offer and final controller intent keep their existing explicit idempotencyKey fields. Require one consumed acceptance for its exact offer/target/nonce and full predecessor; equal original retry only returns retained outcome, never performs another handoff or refreshes deadline/consent. Correct prose that assigns an unlisted key to acceptance.\n\nController factory mutation request Digest means SHA-256 of UTF8(\"artroom-intent-1\\n\") plus canonicalBytes of the unsigned dedicated SiteFactoryIntent, exactly the existing intent-domain framing. Validate the separate closed factory schema first; shipped Intent/FieldValue and ordinary scope-route kinds remain unchanged, with no cast through their nullable-field limits. The seed cause, original ledger request, controller factory receipt request and original-request lookup use that digest. Retain the exact signed envelope as a separate canonical ArtifactRef and verify its actor/signature association to the unsigned intent bytes; its raw artifact digest or signature is never substituted for the intent digest. Factory-read/current-use/borrow answers use the digest of their own unsigned payload under their own declared domain, with consumer-specific meaning explicit. No universal request hash or invented new mutation framing.\n\nBindingDecision is the immutable selected decision digest in binding-domain bytes. Position.revision